4512
03:51:50,720 --> 03:51:51,400
Blast first.

4513
03:51:52,080 --> 03:51:53,320
There we go, and now...

4514
03:51:56,380 --> 03:51:56,780
Engine!

4515
03:51:58,880 --> 03:51:59,280
Sick!

4516
03:51:59,960 --> 03:52:01,240
Hold on, I don't wanna ponder it yet.

4517
03:52:01,320 --> 03:52:01,980
I wanna see it first.

4518
03:52:06,310 --> 03:52:06,710
Fuel?

4519
03:52:06,870 --> 03:52:07,070
None.

4520
03:52:07,230 --> 03:52:07,930
I knew it.

4521
03:52:12,360 --> 03:52:16,600
I'm guessing we can put whatever fuel we normally put in a furnace, you know?

4522
03:52:17,360 --> 03:52:18,180
But let's see.

4523
03:52:20,420 --> 03:52:22,260
It generates rotational force by burning fuel.

4524
03:52:22,560 --> 03:52:23,040
Lovely!

4525
03:52:24,480 --> 03:52:24,960
Coal?

4526
03:52:25,120 --> 03:52:25,300
Yep!

4527
03:52:26,400 --> 03:52:27,300
Sick, man!

4528
03:52:29,080 --> 03:52:30,200
That is awesome!

4529
03:52:32,900 --> 03:52:35,300
It can be configured to run in either direction.

4530
03:52:35,600 --> 03:52:36,100
Oh, nice.

4531
03:52:37,460 --> 03:52:38,220
Very cool.

4532
03:52:42,450 --> 03:52:44,270
Fuel can be inserted by automated means.

4533
03:52:44,730 --> 03:52:45,290
Oh, okay.

4534
03:52:49,460 --> 03:52:51,660
Now you start to appreciate renewable energy.

4535
03:52:52,800 --> 03:52:54,540
So you don't have to do this, you know?

4536
03:52:54,700 --> 03:52:57,400
But I guess this makes sense for something like a train.

4537
03:52:58,220 --> 03:53:02,480
Using a blaze cake, the portable engine can be superheated for additional power output.

4538
03:53:03,560 --> 03:53:04,100
Alright.

4539
03:53:06,140 --> 03:53:07,440
Guess I'll make a blaze cake.

4540
03:53:11,460 --> 03:53:12,060
Nice.

4541
03:53:13,040 --> 03:53:14,140
That is incredible.

4542
03:53:15,360 --> 03:53:19,080
Unfortunately, there was nothing that popped up that sounded like a train.

4543
03:53:20,780 --> 03:53:22,140
I can't believe it.

4544
03:53:26,120 --> 03:53:29,260
Maybe I need to make some of these weird redstone thingies, actually.

4545
03:53:31,700 --> 03:53:34,100
Like, maybe a stock link or something.

4546
03:53:37,440 --> 03:53:38,720
I think I can make that.

4547
03:53:41,860 --> 03:53:42,920
No, I can't.

4548
03:53:44,760 --> 03:53:47,580
Transmitter, copper sheet, lightning rod.

4549
03:53:48,140 --> 03:53:49,820
I believe I needed that for that.

4550
03:53:50,020 --> 03:53:51,820
And copper sheet, I have not.

4551
03:53:52,460 --> 03:53:52,960
Damn.

4552
03:53:55,560 --> 03:53:56,400
Yes, I do!

4553
03:53:56,500 --> 03:53:56,800
Yes, I do!

4554
03:54:04,250 --> 03:54:05,310
What did I say?

4555
03:54:08,340 --> 03:54:08,940
Hmm...

4556
03:54:08,940 --> 03:54:09,740
Stock.

4557
03:54:11,240 --> 03:54:12,080
Item bolt.

4558
03:54:12,540 --> 03:54:14,420
But I also needed the transmission thingy.

4559
03:54:19,950 --> 03:54:21,130
Item bolt.

4560
03:54:21,490 --> 03:54:22,090
I have it.

4561
03:54:22,370 --> 03:54:22,530
Yeah.

4562
03:54:25,250 --> 03:54:26,210
Stock link.

4563
03:54:26,910 --> 03:54:27,530
Oh!

4564
03:54:27,850 --> 03:54:28,490
Look at that!

4565
03:54:30,190 --> 03:54:32,990
Doesn't look like a train, though, but okay.

4566
03:54:40,860 --> 03:54:42,700
When placed, the stock links can...

4567
03:54:42,700 --> 03:54:44,620
Or create a new stock network.

4568
03:54:46,440 --> 03:54:47,320
Wait, really?

4569
03:54:49,480 --> 03:54:50,620
I can invest?

4570
03:54:52,820 --> 03:54:56,240
Right click an existing link before placing it to bind them.

4571
03:55:01,440 --> 03:55:03,060
What, these are antennas?

4572
03:55:12,560 --> 03:55:13,240
Or...

4573
03:55:13,240 --> 03:55:16,800
Stock linked packagers make their inventory available to the...

4574
03:55:16,800 --> 03:55:18,340
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

4575
03:55:20,120 --> 03:55:21,300
Are you saying?

4576
03:55:22,360 --> 03:55:24,960
Oh, that's insane if that's true.

4577
03:55:28,010 --> 03:55:30,630
You're saying I can have a central place with all my stuff?

4578
03:55:31,670 --> 03:55:34,550
And I can have little chests spread around?

4579
03:55:35,310 --> 03:55:36,570
Able to access it?

4580
03:55:37,830 --> 03:55:38,470
Whoa!

4581
03:55:39,490 --> 03:55:41,510
That is absolutely huge!

4582
03:55:47,000 --> 03:55:50,580
Other components on the network can now find and request their items.

4583
03:55:53,000 --> 03:55:53,560
Huh!

4584
03:55:54,960 --> 03:55:57,340
Maybe it's not instant, maybe it needs to be transported.

4585
03:55:58,000 --> 03:55:58,560
Packages?

4586
03:55:58,800 --> 03:55:59,000
Maybe.

4587
03:55:59,660 --> 03:56:00,220
Right?

4588
03:56:03,510 --> 03:56:04,350
Yeah, look!

4589
03:56:04,350 --> 03:56:08,490
On request, items from the inventories will be placed into packages.

4590
03:56:09,010 --> 03:56:09,110
Yeah?

4591
03:56:12,550 --> 03:56:13,150
Alright.

4592
03:56:14,450 --> 03:56:18,110
Stock link signals have unlimited range, but packages require transportation.

4593
03:56:18,110 --> 03:56:19,330
Yeah, how does that work then?

4594
03:56:22,620 --> 03:56:25,240
Full redstone power will stop a link from broadcasting.

4595
03:56:30,390 --> 03:56:34,090
Analog power lowers the priority of a link causing others to act first.

4596
03:56:34,990 --> 03:56:35,830
Yeah, okay, but...

4597
03:56:36,730 --> 03:56:38,670
How am I transporting the packages?

4598
03:56:39,830 --> 03:56:40,390
Drones?

4599
03:56:41,270 --> 03:56:42,810
Amazon delivery or something?

4600
03:56:42,990 --> 03:56:44,430
I don't know, don't they do drones nowadays?

4601
03:56:45,390 --> 03:56:46,610
I think that's only in the US.

4602
03:56:50,860 --> 03:56:51,420
Damn.

4603
03:56:52,440 --> 03:56:53,000
Well...

4604
03:56:53,000 --> 03:56:53,980
What's that sound?

4605
03:56:57,360 --> 03:56:59,860
Oh, it's because there's kids playing outside.

4606
03:56:59,860 --> 03:57:01,980
I kept hearing someone going...

4607
03:57:02,560 --> 03:57:04,540
And I thought it was Jackie, just singing.

4608
03:57:04,920 --> 03:57:05,720
Like she does.

4609
03:57:06,900 --> 03:57:08,400
But it's actually kids outside.

4610
03:57:11,160 --> 03:57:12,320
There's a little playground.

4611
03:57:12,740 --> 03:57:13,360
And it's...

4612
03:57:13,360 --> 03:57:15,980
Kind of annoying actually, that it's right outside my window, but you know.

4613
03:57:17,120 --> 03:57:17,860
It is what it is.

4614
03:57:20,400 --> 03:57:21,220
Small tires.

4615
03:57:24,180 --> 03:57:25,160
Fix all this.

4616
03:57:25,500 --> 03:57:26,740
We got the spring.

4617
03:57:28,820 --> 03:57:30,240
You know what would be really cool?

4618
03:57:31,600 --> 03:57:34,520
If wearing these glasses would allow me to...

4619
03:57:35,960 --> 03:57:36,800
Preview the chests.

4620
03:57:37,020 --> 03:57:37,320
You know what I mean?

4621
03:57:37,380 --> 03:57:39,980
Like I look inside and I go like a little preview of what's inside.

4622
03:57:41,360 --> 03:57:42,680
Ah, how would that even work?

4623
03:57:42,720 --> 03:57:43,700
I don't even know how that would work.

4624
03:57:44,360 --> 03:57:45,360
Yeah, that's probably a bad idea.

4625
03:57:45,540 --> 03:57:46,240
But yeah, I don't know.

4626
03:57:48,080 --> 03:57:50,100
I mean, I guess I put names on them, so it's fine.

4627
03:57:51,500 --> 03:57:52,020
Ah, never mind.

4628
03:57:52,080 --> 03:57:52,420
Bad idea.

4629
03:57:52,900 --> 03:57:53,520
Doesn't make sense.

4630
03:57:54,800 --> 03:57:56,560
The stock link though is kind of interesting.

4631
03:57:56,740 --> 03:57:57,520
This seems big.

4632
03:58:01,480 --> 03:58:03,340
Oh yeah, we also have a clockwork bearing.

4633
03:58:04,280 --> 03:58:05,260
To make a clock.

4634
03:58:06,700 --> 03:58:07,140
Good.

4635
03:58:13,400 --> 03:58:14,680
Well, I'm gonna ponder that.

4636
03:58:15,160 --> 03:58:15,380
Literally.

4637
03:58:15,840 --> 03:58:16,440
For next time.

4638
03:58:17,060 --> 03:58:18,500
Because we are close to trains.

4639
03:58:18,660 --> 03:58:19,140
I can feel it.

4640
03:58:22,390 --> 03:58:23,750
We are almost there.

4641
03:58:27,050 --> 03:58:27,870
But you know what?

4642
03:58:27,870 --> 03:58:29,710
I think we discovered a lot of new stuff today.

4643
03:58:30,370 --> 03:58:32,170
The elevator is now in full swing.

4644
03:58:32,450 --> 03:58:32,850
Literally.

4645
03:58:33,510 --> 03:58:36,610
We have an automated farm on top of the house.

4646
03:58:37,190 --> 03:58:38,630
Harvesting all kinds of goodies.

4647
03:58:39,370 --> 03:58:41,830
We have made a portable engine.

4648
03:58:42,270 --> 03:58:45,730
And we've experimented with assembling things in a sequence.

4649
03:58:46,010 --> 03:58:46,690
Which is awesome.

4650
03:58:49,270 --> 03:58:51,310
That is such a cool way of doing it, by the way.

4651
03:58:51,310 --> 03:58:53,890
So you have the belt system in place, you know.

4652
03:58:54,770 --> 03:58:57,710
And you want people to experiment with the belt and stuff.

4653
03:58:58,130 --> 03:59:01,110
So obviously you wanna have them use them.

4654
03:59:01,730 --> 03:59:05,070
What better way to do it than force them to make something in a sequence.

4655
03:59:05,610 --> 03:59:07,310
I think that's fantastic.

4656
03:59:09,110 --> 03:59:09,770
Love it.

4657
03:59:12,350 --> 03:59:13,130
What do you think?

4658
03:59:18,930 --> 03:59:20,450
Thinks Oliver should watch the eclipse.

4659
03:59:20,650 --> 03:59:21,210
Oh yeah, true!

4660
03:59:21,690 --> 03:59:23,110
Wait, isn't that, like, very soon?

4661
03:59:23,370 --> 03:59:25,590
I guess I'll find out when it becomes really dark.

4662
03:59:27,410 --> 03:59:29,190
Let me google it real quick.

4663
03:59:29,370 --> 03:59:29,790
Click again.

4664
03:59:30,030 --> 03:59:31,090
Real quick.

4665
03:59:32,330 --> 03:59:32,770
Eclipse.

4666
03:59:35,440 --> 03:59:38,060
Okay, it's not for another hour and ten minutes.

4667
03:59:38,880 --> 03:59:39,660
I have time.

4668
03:59:43,790 --> 03:59:46,850
I can't believe the game didn't give you an achievement for time traveling!

4669
03:59:46,850 --> 03:59:47,390
I know!

4670
03:59:48,630 --> 03:59:49,630
What are you- By the way!

4671
03:59:50,470 --> 03:59:51,870
How did that look to you guys?

4672
03:59:51,950 --> 03:59:52,650
That whole sequence.

4673
03:59:52,790 --> 03:59:54,050
I need to rewatch that.

4674
03:59:54,730 --> 03:59:56,190
I gotta see what happened there.

4675
03:59:58,370 --> 04:00:00,410
I think I- I think I banked my table.

4676
04:00:01,250 --> 04:00:03,490
Cause I was a little upsetty spaghetti at dying.

4677
04:00:04,210 --> 04:00:07,970
Walked out and that banging had apparently started the music and also crashed the game.

4678
04:00:10,550 --> 04:00:11,930
So I don't know...

4679
04:00:17,430 --> 04:00:18,590
It looked normal?

4680
04:00:18,850 --> 04:00:19,190
Really?

4681
04:00:20,750 --> 04:00:23,650
You got so angry you decided to invent a TARDIS.

4682
04:00:25,250 --> 04:00:27,010
Honestly, I wasn't really that angry.

4683
04:00:27,170 --> 04:00:28,250
It was more like, oh, come on.

4684
04:00:28,490 --> 04:00:30,770
Did I really do that again feeling?

4685
04:00:31,930 --> 04:00:34,750
It was more like a giant disappointment in myself.

4686
04:00:35,190 --> 04:00:36,250
That's what that was.

4687
04:00:40,490 --> 04:00:41,690
Good script, thank you.

4688
04:00:41,890 --> 04:00:43,010
We worked hard on this one.

4689
04:00:44,250 --> 04:00:45,590
I have a whole team of writers.

4690
04:00:50,660 --> 04:00:51,460
Magical banging?

4691
04:00:51,600 --> 04:00:52,440
What are you talking about?

4692
04:00:53,860 --> 04:00:55,900
Can you consider getting the apple skin mod?

4693
04:00:56,000 --> 04:00:56,460
What is that?

4694
04:00:56,600 --> 04:00:58,320
I'm not gonna add any more mods, I don't think.

4695
04:01:00,820 --> 04:01:01,820
Apple skin mod.

4696
04:01:07,130 --> 04:01:08,650
Food related HUD improvements?

4697
04:01:12,420 --> 04:01:13,400
I think I'm fine.

4698
04:01:13,560 --> 04:01:15,100
I don't need food related HUD improvements.

4699
04:01:17,680 --> 04:01:19,020
If anything, I need...

4700
04:01:20,660 --> 04:01:21,300
I don't know.

4701
04:01:21,420 --> 04:01:22,220
I need...

4702
04:01:23,160 --> 04:01:25,920
Just a better grasp on how to handle my inventory.

4703
04:01:32,130 --> 04:01:33,530
Just for saturation meter?

4704
04:01:33,610 --> 04:01:34,390
I don't even know what that is.

4705
04:01:38,280 --> 04:01:39,380
Did you finish the elevator?

4706
04:01:39,480 --> 04:01:39,760
Almost!

4707
04:01:40,020 --> 04:01:42,120
I mean, it's not exactly where I want it to be.

4708
04:01:42,640 --> 04:01:46,340
I still have a little hack installed, preventing it from going further up.

4709
04:01:46,700 --> 04:01:49,140
But there is most definitely a way to do it without that.

4710
04:01:49,980 --> 04:01:53,380
Especially if you have multiple levels that you want to get to with the elevator.

4711
04:01:53,920 --> 04:01:55,260
Let's say you want to go to the first floor.

4712
04:01:55,380 --> 04:01:56,300
You click one button.

4713
04:01:56,800 --> 04:01:58,180
A second floor, another button.

4714
04:01:58,940 --> 04:02:01,180
I'm gonna implement that at some point.

4715
04:02:01,500 --> 04:02:03,040
It's definitely possible, somehow.

4716
04:02:05,780 --> 04:02:10,300
Especially now that we know we can make, like, redstone over distances, right?

4717
04:02:10,520 --> 04:02:11,700
There's definitely a way to do it.

4718
04:02:13,540 --> 04:02:15,960
Spaghetti is the fate of every player of any factory game.

4719
04:02:16,160 --> 04:02:17,240
Yeah, at least at first.

4720
04:02:17,480 --> 04:02:20,040
But then, you know, you gotta get the basics down with the spaghetti.

4721
04:02:20,660 --> 04:02:23,400
And then when you have it down, then you can start to optimize the spaghetti.

4722
04:02:23,660 --> 04:02:25,440
Just like code, in real life.

4723
04:02:26,520 --> 04:02:29,500
The first time around, you know, you get it to work, barely.

4724
04:02:30,480 --> 04:02:32,460
You hold it together with duct tape and spit.

4725
04:02:33,000 --> 04:02:35,540
And then you ask yourself, okay, how do we make this nice now?

4726
04:02:36,720 --> 04:02:38,020
At least that's how I code.

4727
04:02:40,560 --> 04:02:44,700
If you try to optimize from the beginning, you're gonna end up doing a lot of work again and again.

4728
04:02:51,160 --> 04:02:56,900
I think you should forget about beauty this season, and focus on the sublime, industrial aesthetic of having shit everywhere.

4729
04:02:57,640 --> 04:02:59,940
I think that's pretty much what I'm practicing right now, though.

4730
04:03:01,260 --> 04:03:02,680
There is pretty much shit everywhere.

4731
04:03:03,900 --> 04:03:05,580
And it's getting worse as time goes on.

4732
04:03:05,720 --> 04:03:08,060
Or better, depending on how you look at it.

4733
04:03:09,340 --> 04:03:10,360
It's part of the charm.

4734
04:03:10,360 --> 04:03:11,660
That's what I keep saying, right?

4735
04:03:12,100 --> 04:03:13,100
It's not perfect.

4736
04:03:13,280 --> 04:03:14,400
It's not elegant.

4737
04:03:14,560 --> 04:03:15,100
It's not smooth.

4738
04:03:15,340 --> 04:03:18,880
It's sort of distorted and messed up and dirty.

4739
04:03:19,440 --> 04:03:20,260
On purpose.

4740
04:03:24,350 --> 04:03:26,030
Stalk Link made me happy.

4741
04:03:27,110 --> 04:03:27,630
Good.

4742
04:03:27,890 --> 04:03:28,810
Made me happy too.

4743
04:03:36,110 --> 04:03:38,170
Add the horse crushing create add-on.

4744
04:03:38,350 --> 04:03:40,830
There's a create add-on for crushing horses?

4745
04:03:42,190 --> 04:03:42,710
Damn.

4746
04:03:42,970 --> 04:03:47,210
Someone must really hate horses that they went through all the trouble of making an add-on for it.

4747
04:03:52,670 --> 04:03:53,890
I think it makes glue.

4748
04:03:54,070 --> 04:03:55,090
Oh, I guess...

4749
04:03:55,570 --> 04:03:57,110
Yeah, you do use horses for glue.

4750
04:03:58,890 --> 04:03:59,910
That's a real thing.

4751
04:04:00,630 --> 04:04:03,170
And apparently you also use horses for licorice.

4752
04:04:03,810 --> 04:04:06,490
We make licorice in Denmark out of horses.

4753
04:04:07,070 --> 04:04:07,830
Not kidding.

4754
04:04:10,870 --> 04:04:12,710
We compress them until they taste good.

4755
04:04:13,970 --> 04:04:14,770
Salty sweets.

4756
04:04:16,290 --> 04:04:16,970
Oh yeah.

4757
04:04:17,230 --> 04:04:17,810
Super nice.

4758
04:04:23,060 --> 04:04:24,640
I love the candy add-ons.

4759
04:04:24,640 --> 04:04:25,260
There's candy.

4760
04:04:25,620 --> 04:04:26,900
Can you become a chocolatier?

4761
04:04:27,520 --> 04:04:30,000
That would fit very well with the factory.

4762
04:04:31,500 --> 04:04:32,440
Willy Wonka.

4763
04:04:35,380 --> 04:04:37,400
I mean, I can already make chocolate, right?

4764
04:04:37,540 --> 04:04:37,880
Apparently.

4765
04:04:38,160 --> 04:04:39,220
There's a bucket of chocolate.

4766
04:04:39,220 --> 04:04:42,040
I'm guessing all I need is some sugar and some cocoa.

4767
04:04:44,460 --> 04:04:45,140
Isn't that...

4768
04:04:45,140 --> 04:04:46,260
Wait, what else goes into chocolate?

4769
04:04:46,980 --> 04:04:48,840
Cocoa, sugar, maybe water?

4770
04:04:49,220 --> 04:04:49,940
Something like that.

4771
04:04:50,960 --> 04:04:51,860
And some other stuff.

4772
04:04:52,740 --> 04:04:54,520
A bunch of additives, obviously.

4773
04:04:56,080 --> 04:04:57,980
There's an add-on that adds roller coasters?

4774
04:04:58,100 --> 04:04:58,720
I'm not surprised.

4775
04:05:00,840 --> 04:05:02,500
That's one of the first things I thought of.

4776
04:05:03,520 --> 04:05:04,360
Makes sense.

4777
04:05:07,150 --> 04:05:10,090
